        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گانا (gānā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. CDIAL lists it under gāpayati, the second form it gives beside gāyati, \"sings\" (CDIAL 4135). The noun \"a song\" is the same word, used for what is sung."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
